const message = 'fix(autonomous-coder): TS1470 false-positive + generalize pilot fallback + engine-never-throws

Root causes of the failed PILOT-2->PILOT-3 live LLM job (ivx-worker-efb46ee9):

1. TS1470 FALSE-POSITIVE in scoped typecheck: the engine ran
   `tsc --noEmit --module nodenext` on changed files, but nodenext
   rejects `import.meta` (used at line 310 of the engine file and many
   backend modules) with TS1470. Every LLM patch that touched a file
   using import.meta was falsely rejected as a type error, so the loop
   revised until MAX_ITERATIONS and returned BLOCKED with no commit.
   FIX: switch all scoped typecheck commands to
   `--module esnext --moduleResolution bundler`, which allows
   import.meta (valid in the actual node+tsx / bun runtime) while still
   catching REAL type errors (verified with an injected type error).

2. PILOT FALLBACK TOO NARROW: the deterministic fallback was hardcoded
   to AUTONOMOUS-CODER-PILOT-1 -> AUTONOMOUS-CODER-PILOT-2 only. The
   owner\'s next pilot goal (PILOT-2 -> PILOT-3) did not match
   isPilotLabelChangeGoal, so it fell through to the LLM path and hit
   bug #1. FIX: generalize the fallback to ANY adjacent transition
   PILOT-N -> PILOT-(N+1). extractPilotLabelPair() parses the goal for
   two distinct adjacent pilot labels; findPilotSentinelFile() builds a
   definition regex for the FROM label; deterministicPilotFallback()
   applies the exact-replacement. The controlled-pilot invariant
   (single sentinel-definition file, adjacent-only transition) is
   preserved.

3. ENGINE THREW INSTEAD OF RETURNING A BLOCKED PROOF: when the engine
   threw anywhere in the inspect/plan/patch loop, the worker\'s
   top-level catch stored result=null with NO diagnostic trail (no
   iterations, no commandsRun, no filesInspected). This is why the
   failed job had result=null. FIX: wrap runIVXAutonomousCoder in a
   top-level try/catch that converts any thrown error into a FAILED
   proof with the error message, so the worker always stores a full
   proof with diagnostic state.

Verified: bun test backend/ 1572 pass / 0 fail (5888 expects);
bun x tsc --noEmit 0 errors; autonomous-coder tests 25/25 pass.';

async function commitOne(filePath, content, msg) {
  const gz = gzipSync(Buffer.from(content, 'utf8')).toString('base64');
  const res = await fetch('https://api.ivxholding.com/api/ivx/developer-deploy/action', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Authorization: `Bearer ${ownerAt}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      action: 'github_commit_file',
      input: { path: filePath, content: gz, contentEncoding: 'gzip-base64', message: msg },
      confirm: true,
      confirmText: 'CONFIRM_IVX_GITHUB_WRITE',
    }),
  });
  const text = await res.text();
  console.log(`HTTP ${res.status} for ${filePath}`);
  try {
    const j = JSON.parse(text);
    console.log(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2).slice(0, 800));
    return j;
  } catch {
    console.log('raw:', text.slice(0, 500));
    return { raw: text };
  }
}

// Single commit for the one changed file (all 3 fixes are in this file).
const result = await commitOne(files[0].path, files[0].content, message);
console.log('DONE');
